1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,051
You got a raise. So why are you still broke?

2
00:00:03,321 --> 00:00:08,327
Nearly half of Americans earning $100K+ say they live paycheck to paycheck.

3
00:00:08,597 --> 00:00:10,666
It's called lifestyle inflation.

4
00:00:10,736 --> 00:00:15,557
Every raise quietly turns into a bigger car, a nicer apartment, more takeout.

5
00:00:15,827 --> 00:00:20,160
And your brain adapts fast. Psychologists call it the hedonic treadmill.

6
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:24,192
The new stuff feels normal in weeks, so you need more to feel the same.

7
00:00:24,462 --> 00:00:28,064
Income goes up. Spending goes up. Savings stay at zero.

8
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:32,272
The fix? Save half of every raise, the day it hits your account.

9
00:00:32,342 --> 00:00:34,667
You'll never miss money you never got used to.

10
00:00:34,937 --> 00:00:37,679
Because if you don't, next year you'll get another raise…
